/**
 * @page implementation_principles Implementation Principles
 * @brief Design rules used by InsightPC.
 * @tableofcontents
 *
 * @section implementation_principles_goal Goal
 *
 * InsightPC favors a thin JavaFX presentation layer over a small service
 * facade. The UI should be easy to scan, OSHI calls should be isolated, and
 * formatting rules should be reusable by both production code and tests.
 *
 * @section implementation_principles_diagram Data ownership
 *
 * @dot
 * digraph Principles {
 *   graph [rankdir=TB, bgcolor="transparent", splines=polyline, nodesep=0.6, ranksep=0.85];
 *   node [shape=box, style="rounded,filled", color="#86b7a4", fillcolor="#effaf5", fontname="Arial", margin="0.12,0.08"];
 *   edge [color="#52616f", arrowsize=0.8, fontname="Arial", fontsize=10];
 *
 *   subgraph cluster_ui {
 *     label="JavaFX presentation";
 *     color="#bfdbfe";
 *     fillcolor="#eff6ff";
 *     style="rounded,filled";
 *     Main [label="MainController\nwindow lifecycle\nrefresh actions"];
 *     Tabs [label="Tab builders\nCPU, memory, storage,\nnetwork, process, and power"];
 *     Controls [label="JavaFX controls\ntables, labels, charts"];
 *   }
 *
 *   subgraph cluster_config {
 *     label="Configuration";
 *     color="#ddd6fe";
 *     fillcolor="#f5f3ff";
 *     Settings [label="AppSettings\npersisted preferences"];
 *     I18N [label="I18N\nresource bundles"];
 *     Theme [label="AppTheme\nAtlantaFX themes"];
 *   }
 *
 *   subgraph cluster_service {
 *     label="System data";
 *     color="#bbf7d0";
 *     fillcolor="#f0fdf4";
 *     Service [label="SystemInfoService\nOSHI facade\nformatting helpers"];
 *     OSHI [label="OSHI APIs\nhardware + operating system"];
 *   }
 *
 *   subgraph cluster_docs {
 *     label="Documentation";
 *     color="#fed7aa";
 *     fillcolor="#fff7ed";
 *     Packages [label="packages.dox\npackage ownership"];
 *     Pages [label="Doxygen pages\nmaintainer guides"];
 *   }
 *
 *   Main -> Tabs [label="creates"];
 *   Tabs -> Controls [label="renders"];
 *   Tabs -> Service [label="queries"];
 *   Service -> OSHI [label="wraps"];
 *   Main -> Settings [label="loads/saves"];
 *   Settings -> I18N [label="locale"];
 *   Settings -> Theme [label="theme"];
 *   Controls -> I18N [label="labels"];
 *   Packages -> Tabs [style=dashed, label="documents"];
 *   Pages -> Main [style=dashed, label="guides"];
 * }
 * @enddot
 *
 * @section implementation_principles_rules Rules
 *
 * - Keep OSHI access behind com.tlcsdm.insightpc.service.SystemInfoService so
 *   controllers do not depend on vendor-specific API shapes.
 * - Keep tab construction in com.tlcsdm.insightpc.controller.tab builders. The
 *   main controller should coordinate tab lifecycle, refresh, and settings
 *   actions rather than owning every table or label.
 * - Keep user-visible strings in resource bundles and access them through
 *   com.tlcsdm.insightpc.config.I18N. New labels must be added for every
 *   supported locale.
 * - Keep theme and locale persistence in com.tlcsdm.insightpc.config.AppSettings
 *   so PreferencesFX remains the single source of persisted UI state.
 * - Keep value formatting close to the data source. Byte sizes, uptime, and
 *   process values should be formatted by the service layer before controls
 *   display them.
 * - Keep tests headless unless a behavior requires JavaFX/TestFX. Formatting,
 *   package model, and configuration tests should not initialize a toolkit.
 *
 * @section implementation_principles_refresh Refresh flow
 *
 * Tab builders should create controls once, then update displayed values through
 * explicit refresh actions. Avoid rebuilding full tab contents during routine
 * refreshes unless a table structure changes. This keeps the application
 * responsive and makes future background refresh scheduling easier to add.
 *
 * @section implementation_principles_i18n Internationalization
 *
 * The default bundle is English, with Simplified Chinese and Japanese bundles
 * kept in sync. Code should not concatenate translated fragments when a full
 * sentence or label is needed; add a dedicated key instead. Locale changes
 * should go through AppSettings and I18N so every view observes the same locale
 * source.
 *
 * @section implementation_principles_errors Error handling
 *
 * OSHI data can be unavailable or platform-specific. Service methods should
 * prefer safe defaults and formatted fallback text over leaking exceptions into
 * JavaFX event handlers. UI code can then render partial system information
 * without blocking unrelated tabs.
 *
 * @section implementation_principles_docs Documentation
 *
 * Public classes should describe their role in the package. Package-level
 * ownership belongs in doxygen/packages.dox, while longer maintainer guidance
 * belongs in these supplemental Doxygen pages. Keep generated documentation out
 * of source control; commit only the configuration and source comments that
 * produce it.
 */
